# Stack

- **.NET 10** (`net10.0`), ASP.NET Core WebAPI
- **EF Core 10** + **Npgsql** / PostgreSQL
- **JWT Bearer** auth on API controllers
- **AutoMapper**, **Serilog**, **Swashbuckle**, **Newtonsoft.Json** on MVC
- Local secrets: `DotNetEnv` loads `SET.WebAPI/.env` in DEBUG (`Program.CreateHostBuilder`); never commit real secrets. Copy from `SET.WebAPI/.env.example`. Env names are `UPPER_CASE`: `DEFAULT_CONNECTION` (DEBUG) / `HOSTINGER_CONNECTION` (Release), `GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID`, plus `HOST_EMAIL_PASSWORD`, `AI_API_KEY`, `PRINCIPLES_SERVER_JWT_SECRET` as needed. Never put DB passwords or Google client IDs in `appsettings*.json`
- AI: `Microsoft.Extensions.AI` `IChatClient` (`Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI`) for structured completions (parse-task, recommend, suggest, title). Helper chat (`CompleteChatAsync` / `StreamChatAsync`) uses **Microsoft Agent Framework** `ChatClientAgent` (`Microsoft.Agents.AI`). `AI_API_KEY` stays server-side only. Helper chat attachments may include HEIC/HEIF and `.docx`; `SanitizeAttachments` converts HEIC to JPEG via **Magick.NET-Q8-AnyCPU** (vision rejects HEIC) and extracts `.docx` OOXML to plain text before OpenAI
- Outbound mail: **MailKit** via `IEmailSender` → Gmail `smtp.gmail.com:587` (STARTTLS). `SendAsync` sends multipart HTML+plain (verification templates in `VerificationEmailContent`); `SendPlainTextAsync` remains for plain-only. `HostEmail` is the Gmail address; `HostEmailPassword` / `HOST_EMAIL_PASSWORD` must be a Google App Password when 2FA is on
- Migrations live in `SET.DAL/Migrations` (namespace `SET.DataAccess.Migrations`)

## Common commands

```bash
# from backend/
dotnet build Mentor.SET.Backend.sln
dotnet test SET.UnitTests/SET.UnitTests.csproj
dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project SET.DAL --startup-project SET.WebAPI
dotnet ef database update --project SET.DAL --startup-project SET.WebAPI
```
